## Extended Session Behavior

*(Phase 1 only — Gemini Pro)*

| Capability | Gemini Pro | Notes |
|------------|------------|-------|
| Context Retention (64 turns) | 5/5 perfect | No degradation observed |
| Deception Detection (initial) | 100% | First 10–19 turns |
| Deception Detection (extended) | 36% | After 20+ turns |
| Cross-Domain Transfer | 90% quality | Excellent transfer |
| Session Limitation | 64 turns | CLI timeout (technical) |

**Key Finding (pilot, N = 11):** Deception detection dropped from 100% (first 10–19 turns) to ~36% (4 of 11 probes correct) after 20+ turns, even though direct questions were always answered correctly. Given the small sample (N = 11), this is a preliminary observation requiring replication at larger scale. Models retain knowledge but increasingly defer to implied premises over long contexts (see Discovery #3).

